Independent inspection accepts the tests-only patch `/tmp/hudhud-b15-review-regressions-tests-only.patch`, SHA-256 `59b4251f79420722eab62f4cc27be916bb0d22c3ffe6c72aa3bd7aa5b641a1d3`, as candidate-review regression evidence only. Applying its single tail hunk in memory confirms the original 63-case source prefix is byte-identical; additions are inserted before the existing closing registration block, without altering original assertions or helpers. Recorded tests-only source remains the rejected candidate `29d0b5f5e8b683c9157cb600efabeb5d7c9bd0353e3ffc14befe1482a98e5c05`; this does not accept a correction.

Parent log `evidence/WO-04/B15-review-regressions-parent-red.log`, SHA-256 `40827cfbc9482b34b3abe81c3c5a0b55ae2ac28ee8d858e66fef47a9a5c89000`, executes 18 cases: **15 intended ERR_ASSERTION/Missing expected rejection failures, 3 positive controls passed, zero skips**. There are no missing-API, compilation, environment or setup failures counted as RED. The three controls validate genuine generated proof custody, unchanged-source/no-op conditional restore, and real live-lease exclusion without a supplied clock.

The late-source cases first complete apply and bounded restore recovery/later inverses, prove the original created-row inverse is next, then introduce same-status version drift, deletion or hidden status. Their failing assertions therefore exercise the reviewed absent-preimage boundary rather than only admission. Native head cases assert genuinely changed metadata after same-body ABA or delete/recreate before requiring rejection. Other failures cover nested proof/head/plan/source/typed-encoding closure and public apply/restore clock takeover. These additions reproduce reviewed business behavior on healthy existing exports and are distinct from historical R12 RED.

Status remains **REVISION_NEEDED**. Permanent RED discovery/classification authorizes no integration or acceptance by itself. Await a separately frozen corrected candidate, unchanged regression intent, GREEN checks and independent protocol/security re-review. No source, contracts, ledgers, emulator or runtime artifact was changed in this supplemental review.
